{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "cam_zm_closure",
  "description": "CAM6 ZM deep convection, stage 2: the closure block (closure, zm_convr.F90:2318-2506, with the subcloud-layer thickness dsubcld of the driver, F90:597-603, carried as the whole-column integral of the masked thickness dp_subcld = dp for k >= mx, else 0, under the trivial measure dz = 1). Model Closure computes the cloud-base mass flux mb from the normalized (per unit mb) fluxes and the CAPE deficit: the subcloud-layer properties eb/dtbdt/dqbdt/debdt/dtldt at the launch level mx (F90:2401-2410), the cumulus heating/drying dtmdt/dqmdt at the updraft top jt (F90:2423-2428) and in the interior (F90:2432-2446; beta = 0, F90:2433, collapses the ql weights to ql(k+1)), the virtual potential temperatures thetavp/thetavm and the CAPE-change integrand dboydt above and below the LCL (F90:2457-2485), the buoyant-energy change dadt = integral of dadt_integrand = dboydt (zf_lo - zf_hi) over the active levels lel <= k < mx (F90:2490-2499; lowered by the ESD whole-column integral rule under the trivial measure dz = 1, the Fortran layer weight being carried in the integrand because both integrals share the one imported rule and its free name dz binds by consumer variable name), and mb = max((capelmt - cape)/tau/dadt, 0), zero when dadt = 0 (F90:2500-2503). The closure consumes the NORMALIZED fluxes (mu/md/mc dimensionless fractions of mb, du in 1/hPa), so the flux parameters here are dimensionless; the dumped mu/md/mc/du are mb-scaled, and the tests feed dump/mb (the mb pin, asserting the dumped mb; du is read at jt < k < mx = 16..31, where du(16) is nonzero on every row and du(17..31) = 0). The lel/lcl/jt/mx region masks of the branch laws live inside the zm_* template bodies, zeroing the inactive levels (the surface_layer_source pattern). The dp = 0.01*pdel conversion (README-cam-zm working identity, pdel dumped in Pa) is carried inside the model. Omitted with justification: the zg and qs arguments of the closure signature are never read by its body (grep-verified); the msg loop lower bound (loops start at msg+1 = 6, F90:2401 etc.) is inactive here because every branch lower bound is lel >= 14 > 6; the mumax flux limit (F90:675-690) is inactive on all 15 rows (verified; the limited value equals the dumped mb, mumax-limited mb = mb_dump); lel/lcl/jt/mx are the dumped indices (parameters - they are computed by other blocks: buoyan_dilute and cldprp, cam_zm_parcel.esm and the future cam_zm_cldprp.esm). Tests: per active step (cam_zm_scal.csv row (step,1) and cam_zm.csv rows (step,1,k)), dsubcld against the dumped column (exact) and mb against the dumped column (worst rel 2.5e-16) from the normalized-flux inputs; the step-18 test runs on the model defaults (every step-18 profile equals a default). Numeric tuples generated by stage1/analysis/zm_parcel_closure_tuples.py. Units: working pressures hPa, fluxes normalized (mu/md/mc dimensionless, du 1/hPa), rates per unit cloud-base mass flux (K/hPa, 1/hPa, m/(s^2 hPa)); constants are the zm_convr_run values (rgas = 287.0423113650487 J/(kg K), grav = 9.80616 m/s^2, cpres = 1004.64 J/(kg K), rl = 2.501e6 J/kg, eps1 = 0.6219705862045155, capelmt = 70 J/kg, tau = 3600 s).",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "eqesm:stage2",
   "model:atmosphere",
   "physics:deep-convection"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Zhang, G. J. and McFarlane, N. A. (1995). Sensitivity of climate simulations to the parameterization of cumulus convection in the Canadian Climate Centre general circulation model. Atmosphere-Ocean 33(3), 407-446."
   }
  ]
 },
